{"name":"Caraïbe","hex":"#795f4d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Caribbean","blocks":[{"text":"The Caribbean is a geo-political region in the middle of the Americas centered around the Caribbean Sea in the North Atlantic Ocean, mostly overlapping with the West Indies. Bordered by North America to the north and also the west through Central America, and South America to the south, it comprises numerous islands, cays, islets, reefs, and banks."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Central_America_and_the_Caribbean_Shaded_Relief_Map.png/330px-Central_America_and_the_Caribbean_Shaded_Relief_Map.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caribbean","wikidata":"Q664609"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Atlantic_continents_at_night_by_VIIRS.jpg/500px-Atlantic_continents_at_night_by_VIIRS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Atlantic_continents_at_night_by_VIIRS.jpg/1280px-Atlantic_continents_at_night_by_VIIRS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Atlantic_continents_at_night_by_VIIRS.jpg/500px-Atlantic_continents_at_night_by_VIIRS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAtlantic_continents_at_night_by_VIIRS.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/13/Languages_of_the_Caribbean.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/13/Languages_of_the_Caribbean.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Pre-Columbian languages of the West Indies. Ci